Chapter: InductionUnsound

 Stage 4b/5 soundness tripwire: a structural-induction proof whose
 step case offers `Refl` where the goal is not reflexive must be
 rejected. For `add n Zero === n` the Succ case subgoal normalizes to
 `Succ (add k Zero) === Succ k`; that holds only via the inductive
 hypothesis `add k Zero === k` (discharged by `cong ih`), NOT by
 reflexivity. Offering `Refl` there asserts `add k Zero` and `k` are
 definitionally equal, which they are not, so the subgoal check rejects
 with CDX2001. If induction ever accepted this, it would prove a FALSE
 theorem for every non-base constructor -- the soundness tripwire.

Section: Nat

  Nat =
   | Zero
   | Succ (Nat)

  add : Nat, Nat -> Nat
  add (a) (b) = when a
   is Zero -> b
   is Succ (n) -> Succ (add n b)

Section: Bad Proof

  claim add-zero-bad : for all (n : Nat), add n Zero === n
  proof add-zero-bad =
   induction on n
    is Zero -> Refl
    is Succ (k) (ih) -> Refl
   qed

Section: Main

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni "unreachable"
  end
